#: ../../source/docs/turtle-mode.rst:5
#: aaf695a2668542c78c5a520f5c7d7ecc
msgid "Turtle Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/turtle-mode.rst:7
#: 57072fda6e844ff980aa913803802f93
msgid "Turtle Mode is a special mode that can be invoked either as a :ref:`flight mode <flight-modes>` via the flight mode switch or as an :ref:`Auxiliary function <common-auxiliary-functions>` assigned to an RC switch (channel). Turtle mode allows a user to attempt to flip the Copter upright, if inverted, by reversing the direction of adjacent pairs of motors and producing thrust to un-invert the vehicle after a crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/turtle-mode.rst:11
#: 53c8e7e91de242329565b469c6221667
msgid "This flight mode is available for multirotors only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/turtle-mode.rst:13
#: 76b282003eb949bfa6f863c20c6203c5
msgid "DShot capable ESCs are required for this mode to function, allowing the DShot reverse command to be sent to the ESCs. :ref:`SERVO_DSHOT_ESC<SERVO_DSHOT_ESC>` must be set to a non-zero value and :ref:`MOT_PWM_TYPE<MOT_PWM_TYPE>` to a DSHOT value also, to allow DShot commands to be sent to the ESC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/turtle-mode.rst:15
#: f9adfd4288d0420badc429043f757f83
msgid "Once in this mode, moving the roll and/or pitch stick of the transmitter away from center will reverse and spin up the designated pair of motors, increasing thrust to maximum at full stick throw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/turtle-mode.rst:17
#: f36c72b067ac4ead81b3a53d9587191e
msgid "The user can quickly jab the transmitter stick to attempt to flip the vehicle upright. Which pair of motors is temporarily reversed and spun up is determined by the direction away from center the stick is moved, as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/turtle-mode.rst:23
#: 1a14c4eb2f87498e9cacab9a931be972
msgid "Once flipped upright, exit the mode for normal operation to resume."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/turtle-mode.rst:26
#: 76245e86eb364b1c9b383908f5f2a672
msgid "continuous operation of motors in the reversed mode may cause either ESC or motor overheating in some cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/turtle-mode.rst:28
#: bbf3d5b3e08a4a889d0786a4449960c7
msgid "Turtle mode cannot be entered unless throttle is zero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/turtle-mode.rst:29
#: f61dc60432594ded9c01d08f6eb4cd23
msgid "Upon entry to turtle mode the motors stay disarmed, but the notfiy LEDs flash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/turtle-mode.rst:30
#: 9a86dec15cf547f4b97128c73db16245
msgid "Raising the throttle, the motors arm, and motors spin. Lowering throttle to zero disarms the motors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/turtle-mode.rst:31
#: 7bdf88492d6f41c1b7178a047a0a32cb
msgid "Motors spin only when throttle is raised"
msgstr ""
